01:30.940 --> 01:35.780
Germany - Grunwald Practice Field

01:41.900 --> 01:46.500
Wow! So all of this is Grunwald's training field?

01:46.510 --> 01:49.270
That's right. We also have a rugby field and a tennis court,

01:49.270 --> 01:51.280
but we still have 15 soccer fields alone.

01:51.280 --> 01:53.210
That's awesome!

01:53.210 --> 01:57.390
Oh! So Wakabayashi-san's spent three years in this incredible environment?

01:57.390 --> 01:58.390
That's how it is.

01:59.140 --> 02:00.620
Wakabayashi!

02:00.620 --> 02:01.530
Captain!

02:01.530 --> 02:03.140
It's been a while!

02:04.230 --> 02:07.650
So you guys also got chosen to represent Japan?

02:07.650 --> 02:09.660
Hey, hey, even you, Ishizaki?

02:09.660 --> 02:11.990
What's that supposed to mean?

02:14.210 --> 02:16.940
It's been a while, Wakabayashi.

02:17.670 --> 02:19.460
Yo, Hyuga.

02:19.460 --> 02:25.420
Sorry to postpone my promise of scoring a goal on you from outside the penalty area.

02:25.420 --> 02:27.040
I'm still keeping it though.

02:27.560 --> 02:29.210
You look confidient.

02:29.210 --> 02:33.300
However, I haven't been staying in 
Germany for three years just for kicks.

02:33.610 --> 02:35.380
That's good, Wakabayashi.

02:35.380 --> 02:39.530
Be sure to show us tomorrow how much your training here's given you.

02:39.530 --> 02:40.360
I will.

02:41.790 --> 02:45.650
It looks as if Tsubasa's shoulder injury kept him from coming after all.

02:46.160 --> 02:48.310
A Japanese team without Tsubasa...

02:48.310 --> 02:53.140
They're 100% sure to lose the game tomorrow.

02:55.180 --> 03:00.340
<b>Humiliating Test Match</b>

02:55.180 --> 03:00.340
<b>Humiliating Test Match</b>

03:00.340 --> 03:02.940
Nankatsu Hospital

03:01.370 --> 03:02.940
How's it looking?

03:02.940 --> 03:05.140
<b>Consulation Room Surgical Section</b>

03:02.940 --> 03:09.180
If it was only up to me, I'd prefer you to rest a bit more, but...

03:09.180 --> 03:10.200
Then...!

03:10.710 --> 03:13.140
Yes, your shoulder's pretty much healed.

03:13.570 --> 03:15.620
Your healing ability's stunning.

03:15.620 --> 03:16.860
Yes!

03:18.370 --> 03:20.810
You're really anxious to get back to playing soccer, aren't you?

03:21.600 --> 03:22.700
I am!

03:23.630 --> 03:28.480
Today, the best under 15 European youth team, Grunwald,

03:28.480 --> 03:33.120
is receiving the Japanese Junior Youth National team, who will be participating in

03:33.120 --> 03:36.220
the International Junior Youth Tournament held in France, for a friendly game.

03:45.730 --> 03:46.860
Mother.

03:46.860 --> 03:47.700
Yes?

03:47.700 --> 03:51.190
I'd like you and dad to come watch my game.

03:51.190 --> 03:55.200
Do that, and you'll surely 
understand what dad feels.

03:57.810 --> 04:00.410
My mom and dad were so close...

04:00.910 --> 04:03.350
If only they could go back to how they were...

04:04.060 --> 04:06.150
Brother!

04:09.100 --> 04:10.450
Brother...

04:10.450 --> 04:13.110
Mommy says she can't come.

04:13.110 --> 04:14.390
I see.

04:15.400 --> 04:16.660
What's Schneider doing?

04:16.660 --> 04:18.230
He's not here yet.

04:18.230 --> 04:19.970
With an opponent like the Japanese team,

04:19.970 --> 04:22.680
I'm sure he'd prefer to just watch it on TV.

04:27.480 --> 04:29.180
Looks to me like he's playing.

04:33.060 --> 04:37.260
During today's game the defenders will have to mark that man.

04:37.260 --> 04:41.450
They say he's the future pillar of the German National team.

04:41.730 --> 04:44.960
He's their ace striker: Karl Heinz Schneider.

04:45.460 --> 04:48.580
So he's the ace striker from Germany.

04:52.380 --> 04:54.040
The game's about to get under way.

04:54.040 --> 04:56.600
It's Grunwald versus the Japanese Junior Youth team.

04:56.600 --> 05:00.100
For Grunwald, there's the star Japanese goalkeeper, Wakabayashi-kun.

05:00.100 --> 05:04.610
But will Japan be able to get a goal past him after his training in Germany?

05:09.860 --> 05:11.800
Oh! Number nine of Japan is pushing forward!

05:11.800 --> 05:14.920
But Schneider's right there blocking his way!

05:15.390 --> 05:16.450
Takeshi!

05:16.450 --> 05:16.980
Yes!

05:19.270 --> 05:21.580
Dad didn't come...

05:22.440 --> 05:23.620
Huh, what happened?

05:23.620 --> 05:25.040
Schneider didn't move!

05:27.820 --> 05:29.420
Here I come, Wakabayashi!

05:29.420 --> 05:33.320
I'll crush you with the Tiger Shot I've developed during the three years you've been gone!

05:34.180 --> 05:36.300
Number nine shoots!

05:38.390 --> 05:40.860
The ball has ruptured!

05:40.860 --> 05:44.340
What an incredible show of power, but a bit lacking in control.

05:44.560 --> 05:47.190
That was just a wake-up call, Wakabayashi!

05:47.190 --> 05:50.340
Next time, I'll be sure to aim for the net!

05:54.970 --> 05:56.770
The game resumes with a goal kick.

05:58.560 --> 05:59.520
It's mine!

05:59.130 --> 06:02.210
The ball's intercepted! What's happening to Grunwald?

06:01.530 --> 06:04.910
That was supposed to be the Tiger Shot, but he didn't even move a muscle.

06:04.910 --> 06:07.820
The legendary Wakabayashi isn't all that impressive, after all.

06:07.820 --> 06:08.680
Bro!

06:08.680 --> 06:11.650
We'll be the ones to score Japan's first goal!

06:11.940 --> 06:13.100
I'm counting on you, Nitta!

06:13.510 --> 06:14.340
Yeah!

06:25.600 --> 06:28.730
This is our Sky Love Hurricane!

06:29.730 --> 06:30.880
W-What?

06:33.820 --> 06:35.240
This time it's my turn!

06:36.160 --> 06:36.900
Here!

06:40.650 --> 06:41.660
Nitta!

06:41.660 --> 06:44.100
Take this! This is my Falcon Shot!

06:45.900 --> 06:47.140
He stopped it!

06:47.140 --> 06:50.840
Wakabayashi deftly caught the shot from Japan's number 18!

06:53.140 --> 06:55.340
All right! It's my turn next!

06:56.200 --> 06:57.330
Razor Shot!

06:59.650 --> 07:01.180
Wh-What was that?!

07:01.180 --> 07:02.340
Splendid!

07:02.340 --> 07:04.660
Wakabayashi read the curve and caught the ball in mid-air!

07:06.570 --> 07:08.980
He clears the ball with a long kick!

07:08.980 --> 07:11.200
Will Grunwald be able to mount a counterattack now?

07:11.200 --> 07:12.020
Another steal!

07:12.020 --> 07:13.820
Grunwald's seems to be error-prone today!

07:13.820 --> 07:17.390
Wakabayashi... As expected, your training in Germany has paid off.

07:17.390 --> 07:19.740
But do you think you can stop this shot?

07:19.760 --> 07:20.580
Eagle Shot!

07:23.460 --> 07:24.230
What?!

07:24.230 --> 07:25.220
Damn it!

07:25.490 --> 07:30.270
Wakabayashi reacts calmly to the powerful long shot from number 12!

07:30.270 --> 07:32.890
He's really living up to his name: the Goalkeeper God from Grunwald!

07:34.660 --> 07:37.040
That keeper's doing pretty good.

07:37.040 --> 07:41.220
But if I were up against those shots, I'd stop them all in front.

07:41.550 --> 07:45.430
So that's the best team from Europe Coach Barbas was talking about?

07:45.430 --> 07:47.000
You wouldn't believe it, seeing them play.

07:47.000 --> 07:48.470
That's because they're just toying with them.

07:49.580 --> 07:51.200
Well, just watch.

07:51.220 --> 07:54.340
The ball goes again to the Japanese Junior Youth team who prepares to attack.

07:54.340 --> 07:56.190
Come on, guys!

07:56.190 --> 07:59.870
Wakabayashi's the only good player for Grunwald!

07:59.870 --> 08:02.430
It's a relaxing game for us on defense.

08:05.580 --> 08:06.580
Over here, Takeshi!

08:08.120 --> 08:08.900
What?

08:09.520 --> 08:12.540
Kaltz steals the pass! He's displaying the fast reflexes he's know for!

08:12.540 --> 08:14.380
It's starting now.

08:15.920 --> 08:18.080
Damn it! Let's take it back right away!

08:19.840 --> 08:21.940
It's about time we go at it, guys!

08:21.940 --> 08:23.560
Yeah!

08:26.630 --> 08:27.540
What...?!

08:27.540 --> 08:29.740
They suddenly got much faster!

08:30.040 --> 08:33.540
Grunwald seems to finally have gotten into rhythm!

08:34.800 --> 08:36.300
What's happening?!

08:39.710 --> 08:42.230
Listen carefully, Japanese Junior Youth team.

08:42.230 --> 08:47.080
We only let you go on the attack to see what you're made of!

08:47.080 --> 08:49.350
What?! To test us, you say?!

08:49.350 --> 08:50.100
Stop talking crap!

08:54.090 --> 08:55.060
Hyuga!

08:55.060 --> 08:56.080
Nice!

09:14.030 --> 09:15.620
Oh, Schneider!

09:15.620 --> 09:20.060
He instantly stops number nine of Japan and takes the ball from him!

09:22.480 --> 09:27.060
He gets past the Japanese players in one stroke thanks to his sharp, brilliant dribbling!

09:27.060 --> 09:31.120
This is it! This is the game of the Young Emperor: Germany's pride!

09:36.010 --> 09:37.800
Goal!

09:37.800 --> 09:39.660
There it is, the Fire Shot!

09:39.660 --> 09:41.460
Hamburg gets the opening score!

09:41.460 --> 09:43.900
What was that shot just now?

09:43.900 --> 09:46.890
I see. Karl Heinz Schneider, eh?

09:46.890 --> 09:48.260
Well done.

09:48.900 --> 09:51.420
Obviously he's able to do it at that level.

09:51.420 --> 09:53.440
What? Damn it!

09:53.440 --> 09:55.660
A goal this fast?

10:07.760 --> 10:08.810
Tsubasa.

10:10.210 --> 10:11.900
I'm finally here!

10:12.860 --> 10:15.250
You've arrived sooner than expected.

10:15.250 --> 10:16.890
How's your shoulder?

10:16.890 --> 10:20.690
Even the doctor was surprised by my healing capabilities.

10:20.690 --> 10:22.110
It's okay, as you can see.

10:22.110 --> 10:25.200
But we didn't plan for you to play

10:25.200 --> 10:27.800
before the International Championship in France ten days from now.

10:27.800 --> 10:32.810
I couldn't wait while the others are already playing world soccer.

10:33.740 --> 10:35.170
That's just like you.

10:35.170 --> 10:38.950
They're playing Grunwald and Wakabayshi today.

10:38.950 --> 10:42.540
We might even be in time for the second half.

10:42.540 --> 10:44.700
What? Against Grunwald?

10:50.620 --> 10:53.620
I see. They're playing that team?

10:56.610 --> 11:00.480
It's in! It's the second goal scored with the Fire Shot!

11:00.480 --> 11:03.670
The Japanese goalkeeper couldn't even lay one finger on the ball!

11:04.820 --> 11:07.470
As soon as it comes close to my hands, the ball gains speed again.

11:07.470 --> 11:10.620
This shot's faster than the captain's Tiger Shot!

11:11.160 --> 11:15.220
Grunwald has started playing their game, and in only a few minutes they've scored two goals.

11:15.220 --> 11:19.180
They don't have the reputation as the number one European team for nothing!

11:21.330 --> 11:24.210
Bastards! They're making fun of us!

11:24.210 --> 11:26.430
They think they've won with only a two goal lead?

11:26.430 --> 11:28.480
Damn them! They're underestimating us!

11:28.480 --> 11:30.450
We're the Japanese Junior Youth team!

11:30.450 --> 11:33.580
Things won't end like this!

11:33.580 --> 11:35.250
Damn right!

11:44.380 --> 11:47.380
It's the visiting Japanese Junior Youth team versus Grunwald!

11:47.380 --> 11:51.710
The fierce Japanese attack early on is completely over, and they're now on the defensive!

11:51.710 --> 11:53.760
This has become a crushing game!

11:55.120 --> 11:56.260
Schneider shoots!

11:57.850 --> 11:59.260
It's in!

11:59.260 --> 12:01.170
It's the third goal for Grunwald!

12:01.170 --> 12:03.170
And all of them have been by Schneider!

12:03.170 --> 12:05.350
He's just scored a hat-trick!

12:05.350 --> 12:07.860
And with that, the first half ends.

12:07.860 --> 12:09.250
They're strong.

12:09.250 --> 12:10.200
Damn it!

12:10.200 --> 12:14.350
Instead of us scoring a goal, we've given up even more!

12:14.350 --> 12:15.500
Don't give up!

12:15.500 --> 12:17.500
We've still got another half left!

12:20.500 --> 12:22.650
They're really fast.

12:22.650 --> 12:24.820
How are we supposed to recover?

12:26.090 --> 12:28.820
Japanese team, fight!

12:33.120 --> 12:34.250
Tsubasa!

12:34.250 --> 12:35.630
It's really Tsubasa!

12:35.630 --> 12:37.380
You came!

12:39.790 --> 12:41.960
So you came, Tsubasa!

12:41.960 --> 12:44.830
So he's the one you're always talking about?

12:44.830 --> 12:47.730
That's him. He's a soccer prodigy.

12:47.730 --> 12:48.900
He's Ohzara Tsubasa.

12:48.920 --> 12:49.870
Guys!

12:49.870 --> 12:52.410
But why are you here?

12:52.410 --> 12:54.710
I wanted to hurry over and play with you guys.

12:54.710 --> 12:57.930
I was so impatient, so here I am!

12:57.930 --> 13:00.290
Is your shoulder okay, Ohzara?

13:00.840 --> 13:02.020
It is!

13:02.020 --> 13:04.580
Really? Play the second half, then!

13:04.580 --> 13:05.570
Yeah, do it!

13:05.960 --> 13:08.640
I'm sorry, but Ohzara won't be able to.

13:11.080 --> 13:12.380
Why not?

13:12.380 --> 13:15.290
Since we hadn't planned for your arrival, Tsubasa-kun,

13:15.290 --> 13:18.180
you're not registered as a player for this game.

13:18.500 --> 13:19.900
No way...

13:21.330 --> 13:23.860
And he came all the way here...

13:23.860 --> 13:26.940
And we might turn things around with Tsubasa-san in the game...

13:26.940 --> 13:29.340
Stop saying such pitiful things!

13:30.410 --> 13:32.430
It's not like we've lost yet!

13:32.430 --> 13:34.820
I'll win this game for sure!

13:35.260 --> 13:36.350
Hyuga...

13:36.350 --> 13:37.420
Hyuga-kun.

13:37.420 --> 13:42.080
He's right. We can't say we won't win because Tsubasa-kun can't enter.

13:42.080 --> 13:43.740
Matsuyama.

13:43.740 --> 13:48.640
We won't be able to always play with the best lineup.

13:48.640 --> 13:53.100
In those cases, we'll have to win with the players available.

13:53.910 --> 13:57.390
That's right, guys. Matsuyama-kun's completely right.

13:57.390 --> 14:00.420
There's still the second half. Do your best and go at it!

14:00.420 --> 14:01.980
All right!

14:01.980 --> 14:03.210
Let's do this!

14:03.210 --> 14:04.620
Yeah!

14:06.610 --> 14:08.620
The second half's started.

14:09.900 --> 14:13.140
The Japanese team is backed into a corner, down three goals.

14:16.400 --> 14:18.670
So Tsubasa can't play.

14:18.670 --> 14:22.420
They're without Tsubasa. They won't have any goals at the end of this half!

14:22.420 --> 14:24.680
What?! Damn it!

14:27.350 --> 14:28.590
We'll win!

14:28.590 --> 14:31.620
We can win for sure, even without Tsubasa!

14:31.620 --> 14:32.640
Sorimachi!

14:36.050 --> 14:37.390
As expected from Schneider!

14:37.390 --> 14:38.980
He breaks up the Japanese attack!

14:38.980 --> 14:40.700
Who's that player?

14:40.700 --> 14:44.050
Karl Heinz Schneider from Grunwald.

14:44.050 --> 14:47.310
He scored all the goals in the first half.

14:47.310 --> 14:51.740
So that's Schneider, the Young Emperor Wakabayashi-kun was talking about?

14:57.510 --> 14:59.250
Schneider launches his Fire Shot again!

14:59.260 --> 15:01.100
Don't underestimate me!

15:01.100 --> 15:02.580
Oh, it was stopped!

15:02.580 --> 15:05.260
That keeper stopped Schneider's Fire Shot!

15:05.260 --> 15:06.500
He blocked it...

15:06.500 --> 15:08.420
Awesome, Wakashimazu!

15:13.380 --> 15:14.380
Wakashimazu!

15:14.100 --> 15:16.900
Oh! It looks as if the Japanese goalkeeper has injured his right hand.

15:17.410 --> 15:19.820
How terrifying that Fire Shot is!

15:20.900 --> 15:22.650
Sub him out immediately.

15:22.650 --> 15:25.160
Wait. I can still go on.

15:25.160 --> 15:27.020
This is a whole new game.

15:27.290 --> 15:28.660
Wakashimazu.

15:28.660 --> 15:31.420
It's impossible in that condition.

15:31.420 --> 15:33.010
Let us take care of the rest.

15:33.010 --> 15:34.500
Captain...

15:36.720 --> 15:37.940
I understand...

15:37.940 --> 15:40.540
Morisaki's replacing Wakashimazu.

15:41.940 --> 15:45.920
Japan changes goalkeeper. And with that the game can resume.

16:00.180 --> 16:01.020
I want to go out there!

16:01.020 --> 16:02.430
I want to play this game!

16:02.430 --> 16:06.200
It doesn't matter which position, I just wanna play!

16:08.090 --> 16:11.310
Forget it. However mortifying, it's a total defeat.

16:11.310 --> 16:14.010
Tsubasa, you're free to laugh.

16:14.010 --> 16:16.380
These are our real capabilities.

16:18.910 --> 16:22.100
Oh, Schneider loses the ball for the first time in the game!

16:22.100 --> 16:23.260
Matsuyama!

16:23.260 --> 16:25.460
This game's not over yet!

16:25.460 --> 16:29.010
We'll give it our all until the final whistle blows!

16:29.010 --> 16:31.770
This is what the Japanese Junior Youth spirit is all about!

16:35.860 --> 16:37.660
We're now in stoppage time.

16:37.660 --> 16:38.940
Hyuga-san!

16:41.700 --> 16:43.610
Go for it, Hyuga-kun!

16:43.860 --> 16:44.830
Hyuga-san!

16:44.830 --> 16:46.140
We're leaving it up to you, Hyuga!

16:46.140 --> 16:47.580
Put it in, Hyuga!

16:47.580 --> 16:50.090
Show us why you're Japan's ace striker!

16:52.100 --> 16:53.380
Here I go!

16:57.530 --> 17:03.020
If we've already lost, I need to at least score a goal with a long shot at Wakabayashi-kun!

17:07.020 --> 17:11.420
They gave me this ball just as I was giving up!

17:11.140 --> 17:14.770
The defenders from Grunwald are hurrying to stop Japan's number nine!

17:14.310 --> 17:15.340
We'll stop him!

17:16.880 --> 17:19.010
Hyuga's feinting?

17:19.010 --> 17:21.740
Do you want that one goal that bad?

17:22.860 --> 17:24.540
Oh, he's lost his balance!

17:24.540 --> 17:25.660
It's mine!

17:27.710 --> 17:30.100
Wow! He somehow manages to dodge the defender!

17:30.550 --> 17:33.220
Uh-oh! He's now one-on-one with the keeper!

17:33.580 --> 17:35.220
Take this!

17:40.380 --> 17:42.740
Wakabayashi didn't move a centimeter!

17:42.740 --> 17:45.940
He let in a goal in the very last minute!

17:46.250 --> 17:47.370
He did it!

17:47.370 --> 17:48.900
We got a goal!

17:48.900 --> 17:51.100
Nice shot, Hyuga!

17:51.100 --> 17:52.180
Hyuga-san!

17:55.270 --> 17:56.640
You ran away.

17:56.640 --> 17:59.740
And here I was thinking you were gonna fire a long shot.

18:00.760 --> 18:02.260
What did you say?!

18:02.260 --> 18:04.020
There was a five goal gap.

18:04.020 --> 18:08.920
You had no chance of winning, but you wanted that one goal that much?

18:08.920 --> 18:09.620
Hyuga...

18:09.620 --> 18:10.620
What?!

18:10.620 --> 18:12.050
Enough of this.

18:12.050 --> 18:16.590
Consider this goal as a present from me, since you came all the way from Japan.

18:17.060 --> 18:23.700
But with this coward as your captain, you'll never win a single game in France! {What a dick!}

18:24.350 --> 18:25.960
Y-You bastard!

18:25.960 --> 18:27.540
Calm down, Hyuga!

18:27.980 --> 18:30.140
Stop it, Hyuga.

18:30.140 --> 18:31.540
Let go of me!

18:31.540 --> 18:32.980
Hyuga-kun!

18:36.260 --> 18:38.310
I got it! Get your hands off me!

18:40.860 --> 18:42.130
This is yours, Matsuyama.

18:51.640 --> 18:53.030
Hyuga-kun...

18:53.860 --> 18:56.730
So it'll be Schneider that needs to be stopped.

18:57.300 --> 18:58.770
Okay, should we go?

19:00.460 --> 19:01.660
Yeah.

19:02.140 --> 19:04.340
How was the game?

19:04.340 --> 19:06.030
Coach Barbas!

19:06.030 --> 19:08.060
It was interesting.

19:08.060 --> 19:12.360
We'll indeed need to look out for that Schneider from Grunwald.

19:12.360 --> 19:14.300
The German team looks like it could be

19:14.300 --> 19:16.660
a tough opponent at the Junior Youth Championship in France.

19:17.020 --> 19:19.000
Is that so? And the Japanese team?

19:19.000 --> 19:19.650
Eh?

19:19.950 --> 19:23.860
How did Japan's number ten, Ohzara Tsubasa, play?

19:26.340 --> 19:30.900
There should have been a player called Ohzara Tsubasa on the Japanese team.

19:31.350 --> 19:34.090
One of my friends thinks

19:34.090 --> 19:38.490
he'll be a formidable opponent for the South American football teams in the future.

19:38.490 --> 19:41.230
That has to be some kind of mistake, Coach.

19:41.230 --> 19:43.970
There was no such breathtaking player on the Japanese team.

19:43.970 --> 19:47.300
Who told you something like that?

19:47.600 --> 19:51.230
The former Brazilian player, Roberto Hongo.

20:01.830 --> 20:05.900
I'm sorry I had you play the role of the bad guy, Genzo.

20:07.950 --> 20:08.760
Don't worry about it.

20:11.610 --> 20:14.950
No matter what, I want you to make them understand

20:14.950 --> 20:19.700
that there's a great wall between Japanese and European soccer.

20:19.700 --> 20:21.540
It doesn't matter how you do it!

20:21.540 --> 20:23.160
I'm counting on you, Genzo.

20:23.160 --> 20:24.910
Please take on this role.

20:25.840 --> 20:28.260
Okay, I understand, Mikami-san.

20:34.410 --> 20:37.100
But are you certain this was the right thing to do?

20:37.440 --> 20:41.160
I mean, you built the whole team around Hyuga.

20:42.500 --> 20:43.880
Don't worry about that.

20:43.880 --> 20:49.030
If a team can't come together after being utterly defeated just once,

20:49.030 --> 20:52.310
it can't hope to get very far.

20:52.310 --> 20:55.140
But Hyuga has come a long way.

20:55.140 --> 20:56.260
He has.

20:57.270 --> 20:59.560
Even though I told him that horrible stuff,

20:59.560 --> 21:02.010
I felt the opposite, and was really happy for him.

21:02.010 --> 21:03.580
Even though they were that far behind,

21:03.580 --> 21:09.190
Hyuga put aside his pride and 
scored a goal for his teammates.

21:09.190 --> 21:10.460
That's true.

21:12.440 --> 21:14.800
By the way, Mikami-san. Have you been thinking about it?

21:15.660 --> 21:23.270
About me taking part in the Junior Youth tourney in France as a representative for Japan?

21:34.360 --> 21:38.610
This good-bye present I got from Coach Kira during training camp

21:38.610 --> 21:40.910
is three times heavier than a normal ball.

21:41.630 --> 21:45.440
I was planning on slowly getting used to it without hurting my leg,

21:45.440 --> 21:47.620
but now that's not gonna happen.

21:47.620 --> 21:52.240
I need to be able to strike this like a normal ball, as fast as possible.

21:52.240 --> 21:56.020
And then I'll make a new shot!

22:02.460 --> 22:08.300
Preview

22:04.040 --> 22:08.260
In the game against Grunwald, we saw the kind of wall the World has built up.

22:08.260 --> 22:09.850
The next game is in Italy.

22:09.850 --> 22:13.300
But Italy suddenly backs out of a friendly game

22:13.300 --> 22:15.690
under the pretext that they can't play a weak team.

22:15.700 --> 22:18.020
I then come flying out on the field without thinking.

22:18.030 --> 22:19.620
Don't underestimate the Japanese team!

22:19.620 --> 22:21.560
Just try and stop me!

22:21.560 --> 22:23.130
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa:

22:23.130 --> 22:24.800
The Glorious Number 10.

22:23.340 --> 22:32.380
The Glorious Number 10

22:24.800 --> 22:25.940
Look forward to it!

22:25.940 --> 22:28.160
Let's aim for tomorrow! Get goal! {Original: Let's score a goal and aim for tomorrow! Get goal!}

22:28.160 --> 22:30.460


22:32.860 --> 22:36.660
tsumiageru jibun no takasa wa

22:32.860 --> 22:36.660
My skill keeps on growing.

22:36.660 --> 22:41.020
dare ni mo kimerarenai

22:36.660 --> 22:41.020
Nobody can measure it.

22:41.020 --> 22:44.660
komiageru jibun no yowasa wo

22:41.020 --> 22:44.660
The weakness that grows inside me,

22:44.660 --> 22:49.020
dare ni mo miserarenai

22:44.660 --> 22:49.020
I can't let anyone see it.

22:49.020 --> 22:56.940
aa tada maketakunai sono kimochi de

22:49.020 --> 22:56.940
Ah. It's just, I feel like I never want to lose...

22:56.940 --> 23:03.020
aa ima susumu yo

22:56.940 --> 23:03.020
Ah. Right now, I'll move forward.

23:08.940 --> 23:12.700
tondekuru koishi wo haratte

23:08.940 --> 23:12.700
I ward off the pebble flying towards me,

23:12.700 --> 23:17.020
bai no hayasa de kaesu

23:12.700 --> 23:17.020
And return it with twice as much speed.

23:17.020 --> 23:20.700
yandeiru kotori wo hirotte

23:17.020 --> 23:20.700
I pick up an ill little bird,

23:20.700 --> 23:25.020
ooki na sora ni kaesu

23:20.700 --> 23:25.020
and return it to the wide open sky.

23:25.020 --> 23:32.980
aa tada maketakunai sono kimochi de

23:25.020 --> 23:32.980
Ah. It's just, I feel like I never want to lose...

23:32.980 --> 23:38.980
aa ima susumu yo

23:32.980 --> 23:38.980
Ah. Right now, I'll move forward.

23:44.460 --> 23:48.980
ima daseru subete no chikara de

23:44.460 --> 23:48.980
Using all the strength I have,

23:48.980 --> 23:52.500
koukai wa shitakunai

23:48.980 --> 23:52.500
without feelings of regret...

23:52.500 --> 24:00.020
ima daseru subete no chikara de saikou no kachi

23:52.500 --> 24:00.020
Using all the strength I have, to the ultimate victory.
